<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungarian Working People's Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hungarian Working People's Party was the ruling communist party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1948 to 1956, formed by the forced merger of the Communist Party with the Social Democrats. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matyas-rakosi">Mátyás Rákosi</a>, it imposed a Stalinist dictatorship. It collapsed during the revolution of October 1956 and was replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janos-kadar">János Kádár</a>'s Hungarian Socialist Workers' Party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungarian-working-peoples-party.jpg" alt="Hungarian Working People's Party" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Hungarian_Working_People%27s_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
